00\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0013 SEQ CHAPTER \\h \\r 1\u0015MINUTES OF A REGULAR MEETING OF\rTHE CITY COUNCIL OF THE CITY OF CALABASAS,\rCALIFORNIA, HELD WEDNESDAY, FEBRUARY 11, 2009\r\rMayor Maurer called the meeting to order at 7:35 p.m. in the City Council Chambers of City Hall, 100 Civic Center Way, Calabasas, California.\r\rROLL CALL Present: Mayor Maurer, Mayor pro Tem Wolfson, Councilmembers Bozajian, Groveman, Washburn.\r Absent: None.\r Staff: Colantuono, Coroalles, Peirce, Rubin, Yalda.\r\rThe Pledge of Allegiance was led by Captain Tom Martin.\r\rAPPROVAL OF AGENDA\r\rMayor pro Tem Wolfson moved, seconded by Councilmember Groveman, to approve the agenda. MOTION CARRIED 5/0.\r\rANNOUNCEMENTS/INTRODUCTIONS \r\rMayor Maurer presented an employee service award to Tony Coroalles for his five years of service to the City of Calabasas. Councilmember Washburn spoke regarding upcoming electronic waste disposal events around the City. Mayor pro Tem Wolfson announced that the City�s Arbor Day Celebration will be taking place on Saturday, March 14, 2009. Councilmember Bozajian spoke regarding the Annual St. Patrick�s Day Open House celebration that will be occurring on Saturday, March 14, 2009. Mayor Maurer announced that the Las Virgenes Unified School District Foundation fundraiser will be taking place on February 22, 2009.\r\rORAL COMMUNICATIONS - PUBLIC COMMENT\r\r Freddie Ravel, spoke regarding his concert event that will be held in the Founders Hall on Friday, February 20, 2009. \r\rCONSENT ITEMS \r\r Approval of the minutes for the January 28, 2009 City Council meeting. \r\r Recommendation to renew a facility use agreement with Little Learners, LLC, for the operation of after school and seasonal camp programs. \r\r Approval of a Professional Services Agreement with General Environmental Management, Inc. for regular cleaning and maintenance of Storm Drain BMP Devices. \r\r Recommendation to approve the fifth amended employment agreement for the City Manager. \r\rCouncilmember Washburn moved, seconded by Mayor pro Tem Wolfson, to approve Consent Items #1, 2, 3 and 4. MOTION CARRIED 5/0. \r\rSPECIAL PRESENTATION \r\r Public Safety update presented by Los Angeles County Sheriff�s Captain Tom Martin. \r\rThere was no action taken.\r\r Special presentation on speed limits in the City of Calabasas.\r\rRobert Yalda, Public Works Director, presented the staff report.\r\rKarl Reinecker, Calabasas, and Andy Howard, Calabasas, spoke in opposition to the 50 mph speed limit that has recently been imposed on Mulholland Highway near Mountain Park.\r\rThe City Council provided direction to the City Manager to re-survey the new 50 m.p.h. speed limit on Mulholland Highway and to investigate the options for traffic calming devices in the area.\r\rNEW BUSINESS \r\r Adoption of Resolution No. 2009-1172, approving City involvement with Los Angeles Regional Interoperable Communication System. \r\rCouncilmember Groveman moved, seconded by Mayor pro Tem Wolfson, to adopt Resolution No. 2009-1172, approving City involvement with Los Angeles Regional Interoperable Communication System with an amendment to the JPA to provide the City Manager with the authority to remove the City from the agreement if the City Council cannot convene in a timely manner. MOTION CARRIED 5/0.\r\rINFORMATIONAL REPORTS \r\r Check Register for the period of January 21, 2009 to January 30, 2009. \r\rThere was no action taken.\r\rTASK FORCE REPORTS\r\r There were no task force reports.\r\rCITY MANAGER�S REPORT\r\r City Manager Coroalles indicated he had nothing to report.\r\rFUTURE AGENDA ITEMS\r\r The City Council requested that an item regarding speed limits on roads where a large difference in speeds exist, an item on economic development and a plan to prepare for potential State and Federal government funding and an item on gray water be placed on a future agenda.\r\r\u0013 SEQ CHAPTER \\h \\r 1\u0015ADJOURN \r\rThe City Council adjourned at 9:50 p.m. in memory of Paul Anik to their next regular meeting, which will be held on Wednesday, February 25, 2009 at 7:30 P.M. \r\r\r\r\r\r\r__________________________________\rGwen Peirce, CMC, City Clerk\r\r\r\r\u0003\r\r\u0004\r\r\u0003\r\r\u0004\r\r\u0013 PAGE \\* MERGEFORMAT \u00142\u0015\r\r\r\u0013 PAGE \\* MERGEFORMAT \u00142\u0015\r02/11/09\r\r\r\r\r\r\r\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u